<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I88aa97bec59267132d7c37989129f39593127576" commit="af0aebce47b203625236f7fee114010cff846157" commit_message="touch_updater: stupdate updater now uses common rebind_driver() function.  Previously this updater script had its own rebind implementation, probably because rebind_driver() used to not support binding a device which didn't successfuly bind on boot, e.g. because its firmware was corrupt.  This now takes advantage of being able to specify the driver to (re)bind the device to.  BUG=b:132830741 TEST=Tested no-update, normal update, and firmware corruption recovery with stupdate touch updater.  All cases succeeded as expected.  Verified by testing basic touch functionality, examining /var/log/messages, and querying the touch controller for its firmware version.  Cq-Depend: chromium:1772378,chrome-internal:1762938 Change-Id: I88aa97bec59267132d7c37989129f39593127576 Signed-off-by: Matthew Blecker &lt;matthewb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1789022 Legacy-Commit-Queue: Commit Bot &lt;commit-bot@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Sean O'Brien &lt;seobrien@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="1789022" owner_email="matthewb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/touch_updater" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/touch_updater" ref="refs/changes/22/1789022/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1982af049844f295f7a96734056a23e48d9b5b2d" commit="db917735029f6abd5433fd6171ffec7317290532" commit_message="chromeos-config: cleanup redundant x86/ARM init code  This refactors the initialization functions of CrosConfig to no longer have separated implementations for both x86 and ARM, treating both as a CrosConfigIdentity, and relies on the underlying CrosConfigIdentityX86 or CrosConfigIdentityArm to handle the architecture dependant sections.  The (many) Init functions of CrosConfig have been simplified down to two:  * Init * InitForTest  An alias of InitModel to Init was provided, to be removed after everything else in platform2 no longer calls InitModel (solved in child CLs).  BUG=chromium:999401,chromium:999403 TEST=sudo FEATURES=test emerge chromeos-config-tools  Change-Id: I1982af049844f295f7a96734056a23e48d9b5b2d Signed-off-by: Jack Rosenthal &lt;jrosenth@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1776072 Legacy-Commit-Queue: Commit Bot &lt;commit-bot@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mathew King &lt;mathewk@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Abe Levkoy &lt;alevkoy@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Simon Glass &lt;sjg@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="4" gerrit_number="1776072" owner_email="jrosenth@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/72/1776072/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id06ec8352174a3416d100b479a82f2c0176c966b" commit="cee9458847ad1a12ef5550694be06ab3922472d4" commit_message="chromeos-config: add fallback to mosys for non-unibuild platforms  On non-unibuild platforms, the config.json file will not be available. Previously, libcros_config would return false for all lookups on these platforms. But we can get some data from mosys platform commands:    cros_config /firmware image-name       =&gt; mosys platform model   cros_config / brand-code               =&gt; mosys platform brand  This adds a fallback interface, only used when config.json is not available (non-unibuild), to call out to mosys for these lookups.  BUG=chromium:991653 BRANCH=none TEST=all of above commands on samus (non-unibuild) TEST=sudo FEATURES=test emerge chromeos-config-tools  Change-Id: Id06ec8352174a3416d100b479a82f2c0176c966b Signed-off-by: Jack Rosenthal &lt;jrosenth@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1761410 Legacy-Com